# Slash commands

When the user types a slash command, dispatch it via MCP — **never Shell it, never ask the user to run it**.

## Workflow modes — read the rule file, then act

| Command | Rule file | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| `/talk` | `.cursor/rules/talk.mdc` | Spawn strategic discussion subagent |
| `/dev` | `.cursor/rules/dev.mdc` | Spawn build subagent |
| `/explain` | `.cursor/rules/explain.mdc` | Spawn explanation subagent |
| `/edit` | `.cursor/rules/edit.mdc` | Spawn surgical fix subagent |
| `/clean` | `.cursor/rules/clean.mdc` | Spawn file-tree cleanup subagent |
| `/wire` | `.cursor/rules/wire.mdc` | Spawn import-wiring subagent |
| `/modular` | `.cursor/rules/modular.mdc` | Spawn packaging subagent |
| `/audit` | `.cursor/rules/audit.mdc` | Spawn three-layer audit subagent |
| `/find <q>` | `.cursor/rules/find.mdc` | Direct hybrid search — no subagent |
| `/read [sub]` | `.cursor/rules/read.mdc` | Direct MCP inspect dispatch — no subagent |

For workflow modes, follow the rule file immediately — it contains the full subagent prompt.

## /read dispatch (inline quick-ref)

`/read <sub>` → `run_command("/read <sub>")`

status · health · context · watchdog · hooks · queue · commands · bus · poll · forecast · coherence · index · hub · ana-chi · graph · clean · nest · track · traverse · vault · vault-store · psspps · find · audit · cairrn · css · m3 · temporal · vector · temporal-coherence · phi · shuffle

## /do dispatch (inline quick-ref)

`/do <sub>` → `run_command("/do <sub>")`

sim · neg-exp · sweep · langevin · mfpt · ana-chi · propagate · inject · reset · hub-inject · set-goal · clear-goal · commit · link · topo · cairrn-topo · ingest · ingest-source · sync · track-sync · annotate · vault-project · vault-migrate · test · cairrn · batch · k · record · advance · temporal-reset · enqueue · step · flush · clip · seed · shuffle-step · next · submit · wait · restart · 10

## Rules

1. Call `run_command(command="/<slash>")` for any `/read` or `/do` sub.
2. For workflow modes, read the `.cursor/rules/<mode>.mdc` file and follow it.
3. Unknown slash → call `list_commands()` or `run_command("/read commands")`.
4. `/cairrn` bare → `hub_state`. `/cairrn HOME 1.0` → `cairrn_hub_run`.
